# Third-party portable runtime (KiCad 10.0.6): vendor redistributable, ~1.4 GB,
# contains a 922 MB installer that exceeds GitHub's 100 MB per-file hard limit.
# Install KiCad from https://www.kicad.org/ instead.
70_tools/runtime_wp09_kicad/

# SolidWorks lock files. SolidWorks writes a ~$<name> stub (~126 bytes) next to
# any document it has open, holding only the owning user/machine. They carry no
# design data, and stale ones make SolidWorks report "file in use by another
# user". 314 of them had been committed; removed 2026-09-22.
~$*

# FreeCAD auto-backups (regenerable, ~132 MB) — excluded only where the
# corresponding .FCStd original is committed alongside them.
*.FCBak
*.fcbak

# EXCEPTION: this history snapshot contains ONLY .FCBak files — no .FCStd
# original exists on disk or in the repo, so these backups are the sole
# surviving copy of the V4 pre-refinement state. Verified 2026-09-22.
!20_engineering/F3R2_V4_COMPETITION_MECHANICAL_CANDIDATE_20260809/12_history/FreeCAD_pre_refinement_20260809/*.FCBak

# NOTE on Windows reserved device names (AUX/CON/PRN/NUL/COM#/LPT#):
# Paths with a reserved name in ANY component can be enumerated but not opened
# by Win32 APIs, so `git add` fails on them with exit 128. Rather than excluding
# that content, the three affected paths were renamed on 2026-09-21 (content
# byte-identical, nothing dropped) — see RENAMES_20260921.md.
